-- 1. The Ksheera Arghyam becomes a numbered sequence of offerings instead of
--    one undifferentiated block of Sanskrit, in both poojas. Each verse now
--    carries the "idam arghyam" refrain that says how many times to pour --
--    the refrains were missing entirely, so there was nothing on screen to
--    pour along with.
--
-- 2. Ganesha's four arghyam verses are re-sourced. Migration 0009 wrote three
--    under a source_ref naming a video rather than a text. The Siddhi Vinayaka
--    Vrata Kalpam gives four; two of ours differed from it in the second pada
--    and the third matched no published text. All four here are taken from the
--    cached source page and round-trip verified Telugu -> Devanagari -> Telugu.
--
-- 3. Sharadu Dharanam records who ties the thread. The husband ties it on his
--    wife's right wrist with three knots; the step said only "an elder in the
--    house". Household practice, not kalpam text, and labelled as such.
--
-- Idempotent.
-- =============================================================================

